{
    "$comment": [
        "The route crawl of the HTTP differential replay (docs/http-replay.md). Every entry is requested as every role in 'roles' (default: all), in this order, on a freshly initialised portal.",
        "The routes come from uPortal's servlet-side controller mappings (33 deployed controller classes, see 'Route sources' in docs/http-replay.md) and the portal URL syntax.",
        "Path-matching variants (trailing slash, .json/.xml suffix, a dot in the last path variable) are listed on purpose: Spring 6 removes suffix pattern matching and trailing-slash matching.",
        "Portlet pages are generated from 'portlets' x 'portletStates'. Portlets that fetch content from the internet (RSS, LTI, web proxy) are left out, so the recording does not depend on other sites.",
        "Groups are named by their PAGS key (pags.Authenticated Users), never by a local.N key: local group ids are generated, and differ between machines (docs/http-replay.md).",
        "Entries with 'probe': 'csrf' change state, or would if they were valid; they run last, are built to change nothing in 5.17 (unknown ids, empty bodies), and are what the CSRF section of the security report shows."
    ],
    "portletStates": ["max", "exclusive"],
